Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:53:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 169/175] fix: film grain kept the linear mean and so tinted
 the picture - keep the encoded mean instead

With Film's per-layer amplitudes (B 1.3 / G 0.9 / R 1.0) the picture turned yellow. The
blend is a log-normal, x * 2^(g n), and the bias term preserved the LINEAR mean; what the
eye and an 8-bit capture average is the display-ENCODED value, and a right-skewed
log-normal whose linear mean is held loses encoded mean in proportion to g^2 - most in
the strongest layer, blue. The bias is now the moment of the encoded value, (g/2.4)^2 ln2/2,
so a grey card keeps its code value per channel. Spec section 3 and R2.4 amended.

